<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:vm="using:WhisperNotes.App.ViewModels"
             xmlns:dd="using:WhisperNotes.App.DesignData"
             xmlns:controls="using:WhisperNotes.App.Views.Controls"
             mc:Ignorable="d"
             x:Class="WhisperNotes.App.Views.CaptureBarView"
             x:DataType="vm:MainWindowViewModel"
             d:DataContext="{x:Static dd:DesignTime.Main}">

  <!--
    ==========================================================================================
    Capture bar — ONE row.

    It used to be a three-column block ~180px tall: a stack of section labels, a channel
    detail line, a model picker with a reserved progress strip, session/project inputs and a
    "NOT RECORDING" explainer card. That is a quarter of the window spent before the first
    transcript line, and most of it restated what the status bar already says.

    Everything StatusBarView already carries has been deleted rather than relocated:
      * the primary monitored-input detail ("LOOPBACK · native 44.1 kHz · stereo · resampled
        to 16 kHz") — StatusBarView column 1 renders it verbatim; the toolbar now shows the
        enabled-input count and opens the dedicated Inputs page
      * the model status ("base · on disk") — StatusBarView column 0, dot and all; the model
        picker's own item template repeats it per row anyway
      * the INPUTS / WHISPER MODEL / SESSION section headings — labels and the
        controls' own shapes say the same thing in a row that is read left to right
      * the "NOT RECORDING" card — pure prose, and the record button's own label and colour
        already state the transport's state
      * the model download progress — StatusBarView column 3, next to the video-import
        progress it is visually identical to. Downloading weights is a background operation,
        not a transport control, and reserving a strip for it under the picker centred the
        picker 8px above every other control on this row.

    HEIGHT IS PINNED, deliberately (CaptureBarRowHeight). This bar sizes the row above the
    transcript ScrollViewer; if it changes height at runtime, the viewport is resized under a
    stationary scroll offset and the transcript loses its place. A fixed row height makes that
    impossible by construction: no state change — recording, downloading, a silent channel, a
    long device name — can move it, because nothing in here is allowed to measure taller than
    the row.

    WIDTH IS BUDGETED, for the same class of reason. MainWindow's MinWidth is 1040 and a Grid
    does not scroll, so anything past the window is simply clipped off the right edge — which
    is where the record button lives. Every column below is either a star that gives way or a
    hard floor listed here, and the floors sum to 996:

      toolbar Padding (PadControl 10,6)                                 20
      7 x ColumnSpacing Space3                                          56
      col 0  INPUTS summary       ChannelMinWidth                       88
      col 1  refresh              RowControlHeight square               28
      col 2  level meter          well 108 + Space3 + readout 64       180
      col 3  model                ModelComboWidth 140 + Space2 + 28    172
      col 4  session title        SessionMinWidth                       88
      col 5  project              ProjectWidth                          88
      col 6  transport / import   TransportSlotWidth                   120
      col 7  record               RecordMinWidth                       160
                                                                      ====
                                                                      1000

    It was 1359 idle and ~1422 with a silent channel, against a 1360px default window. No
    state change adds to the total any more: the meter's silence warning replaces its readout
    instead of appearing beside it, the transport shares a fixed cell with the import button
    (they are mutually exclusive), and the record button has a floor wide enough for its
    longest label so pressing it cannot shrink it out from under the pointer.
    ==========================================================================================
  -->

  <UserControl.Resources>
    <!-- Bar geometry. Named rather than inline so no raw number appears in the markup. -->
    <x:Double x:Key="CaptureBarRowHeight">32</x:Double>

    <!-- ONE content height for the row. App.axaml ships three (Button.icon 26, Button/TextBox/
         ComboBox 28, Button.record 38), so their centres lined up and their edges did not;
         until there is a ControlHeight token to share, the row pins them in its own styles. -->
    <x:Double x:Key="RowControlHeight">28</x:Double>

    <!-- Button.record's 16,9 padding is what forces its 38px box. The row height decides now,
         so the padding is only there to keep the label off the edges. -->
    <Thickness x:Key="PadRecord">16,2</Thickness>

    <!-- Column geometry. ColumnDefinition.MinWidth is a plain double, so these can be tokens;
         the two star weights are GridLengths and are written inline below. -->
    <x:Double x:Key="ChannelMinWidth">88</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="SessionMinWidth">88</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="ProjectWidth">88</x:Double>

    <!-- Fixed, not Auto: a ComboBox measures the selected item only, so an Auto column would
         re-lay the whole toolbar out every time the model changed. -->
    <x:Double x:Key="ModelComboWidth">140</x:Double>

    <!-- Fits the widest of the three things that share the cell: "Import video…",
         "Cancel import", and the dot + 00:00:00 clock. Rounded up rather than fitted exactly:
         a floor that is a few pixels short of the widest state reserves nothing. -->
    <x:Double x:Key="TransportSlotWidth">120</x:Double>

    <!-- Fits "Start recording" at FontSizeLg SemiBold, so "Starting…", "Stopping…" and "Stop"
         cannot shrink the button out from under the pointer that just pressed it. -->
    <x:Double x:Key="RecordMinWidth">160</x:Double>

    <x:Double x:Key="ModelDotSize">6</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="RecordDotSize">9</x:Double>
  </UserControl.Resources>

  <UserControl.Styles>
    <Style Selector="Button.subtle, TextBox, ComboBox">
      <Setter Property="Height" Value="{StaticResource RowControlHeight}" />
    </Style>

    <Style Selector="Button.icon">
      <Setter Property="Width" Value="{StaticResource RowControlHeight}" />
      <Setter Property="Height" Value="{StaticResource RowControlHeight}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- MinHeight as well as Height: Avalonia clamps a measured height up to MinHeight after
         applying Height, so the 38 in App.axaml would win on its own. -->
    <Style Selector="Button.record">
      <Setter Property="Height" Value="{StaticResource RowControlHeight}" />
      <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="{StaticResource RowControlHeight}" />
      <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="{StaticResource RecordMinWidth}" />
      <Setter Property="Padding" Value="{StaticResource PadRecord}" />
    </Style>
  </UserControl.Styles>

  <Border Classes="toolbar">
    <Grid Height="{StaticResource CaptureBarRowHeight}" ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource Space3}">
      <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
        <ColumnDefinition Width="1.6*" MinWidth="{StaticResource ChannelMinWidth}" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" MinWidth="{StaticResource SessionMinWidth}" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
      </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

      <!-- Recording inputs are configured on their own page; this compact summary opens it. -->
      <Button Grid.Column="0"
              Classes="subtle"
              VerticalAlignment="Center"
              HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
              HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch"
              IsEnabled="{Binding CanEditSessionMetadata}"
              Command="{Binding GoToPageCommand}"
              CommandParameter="{x:Static vm:ShellPage.Inputs}"
              ToolTip.Tip="Configure loopback and microphone inputs captured together">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource Space3}">
          <Border Grid.Column="0" Classes="badge" Classes.loopback="True">
            <TextBlock Text="INPUTS" />
          </Border>
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                     VerticalAlignment="Center"
                     TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                     Text="{Binding Inputs.SummaryText}" />
        </Grid>
      </Button>

      <Button Grid.Column="1"
              Classes="icon"
              VerticalAlignment="Center"
              IsEnabled="{Binding CanEditSessionMetadata}"
              Command="{Binding Inputs.RefreshCommand}"
              ToolTip.Tip="Re-scan all configured inputs — devices come and go"
              Content="&#x21BB;" />

      <!-- ============ Pre-flight level meter ============
           Well, LEDs, peak hold and readout are one component now; this view hands it the one
           binding it needs. -->
      <controls:LevelMeter Grid.Column="2"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           DataContext="{Binding Capture.Meter}" />

      <!-- ============ Whisper model ============ -->
      <StackPanel Grid.Column="3"
                  Orientation="Horizontal"
                  Spacing="{StaticResource Space2}"
                  VerticalAlignment="Center">

        <ComboBox Width="{StaticResource ModelComboWidth}"
                  VerticalAlignment="Center"
                  ItemsSource="{Binding Capture.Models}"
                  SelectedItem="{Binding Capture.SelectedModel}"
                  IsEnabled="{Binding CanEditSessionMetadata}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="Which whisper weights decode this channel">
          <!-- The closed box shows the dot and the name only. Repeating the per-item status here
               ("not downloaded · 465 MB") squeezed the model's own name out of the control,
               and StatusBarView already states it in full for the selected model. -->
          <ComboBox.SelectionBoxItemTemplate>
            <DataTemplate DataType="vm:ModelOptionViewModel" x:DataType="vm:ModelOptionViewModel">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{StaticResource Space2}" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <Ellipse Width="{StaticResource ModelDotSize}" Height="{StaticResource ModelDotSize}"
                         VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         Fill="{DynamicResource SuccessBase}" IsVisible="{Binding IsDownloaded}" />
                <Ellipse Width="{StaticResource ModelDotSize}" Height="{StaticResource ModelDotSize}"
                         VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         Fill="{DynamicResource TextMuted}" IsVisible="{Binding !IsDownloaded}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              </StackPanel>
            </DataTemplate>
          </ComboBox.SelectionBoxItemTemplate>
          <ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
            <DataTemplate DataType="vm:ModelOptionViewModel" x:DataType="vm:ModelOptionViewModel">
              <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource Space3}">
                <Ellipse Grid.Column="0"
                         Width="{StaticResource ModelDotSize}" Height="{StaticResource ModelDotSize}"
                         VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         Fill="{DynamicResource SuccessBase}" IsVisible="{Binding IsDownloaded}" />
                <Ellipse Grid.Column="0"
                         Width="{StaticResource ModelDotSize}" Height="{StaticResource ModelDotSize}"
                         VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         Fill="{DynamicResource TextMuted}" IsVisible="{Binding !IsDownloaded}" />
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Name}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Classes="caption" Text="{Binding StatusText}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              </Grid>
            </DataTemplate>
          </ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
        </ComboBox>

        <!-- Download and Cancel share one cell, so they overlay instead of stacking: the swap
             changes neither the row's height nor its width. Progress is reported by the status
             bar, which is where every other background operation reports. -->
        <Panel VerticalAlignment="Center">
          <Button Classes="icon"
                  Content="&#x2193;"
                  Command="{Binding Capture.DownloadModelCommand}"
                  IsEnabled="{Binding CanEditSessionMetadata}"
                  IsVisible="{Binding !Capture.IsDownloading}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="Fetch the ggml weights for the selected model" />
          <Button Classes="icon"
                  Content="&#x2715;"
                  Command="{Binding Capture.DownloadModelCancelCommand}"
                  IsEnabled="{Binding CanEditSessionMetadata}"
                  IsVisible="{Binding Capture.IsDownloading}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="Cancel the download" />
        </Panel>
      </StackPanel>

      <!-- ============ Session metadata ============
           Disabled, not hidden, while rolling: the height must not move, and you should still
           be able to read what the session in progress is called. -->
      <TextBox Grid.Column="4"
               VerticalAlignment="Center"
               PlaceholderText="Session title"
               IsEnabled="{Binding CanEditSessionMetadata}"
               Text="{Binding Capture.SessionTitle}"
               ToolTip.Tip="Names the session folder and the notes.md heading" />

      <TextBox Grid.Column="5"
               Width="{StaticResource ProjectWidth}"
               VerticalAlignment="Center"
               PlaceholderText="Project"
               IsEnabled="{Binding CanEditSessionMetadata}"
               Text="{Binding Capture.Project}"
               ToolTip.Tip="Groups sessions — becomes the folder under the notes root" />

      <!-- ============ Transport / recorded-media input ============
           One fixed-width cell for both. Recording and importing are mutually exclusive by
           construction (CanToggleRecording refuses while an import is in flight,
           CanImportVideo refuses while recording), so the elapsed clock takes the cell the
           import button was using instead of appearing beside it — which is what used to slide
           the record button 83px sideways at the instant it was clicked.

           The picker stays in this view because StorageProvider belongs to the TopLevel; the
           selected local path is handed straight back to the view model. -->
      <Grid Grid.Column="6"
            MinWidth="{StaticResource TransportSlotWidth}"
            VerticalAlignment="Center">
        <Panel IsVisible="{Binding !IsRecording}">
          <Button Classes="subtle"
                  Content="Import video…"
                  IsVisible="{Binding !IsImportingVideo}"
                  IsEnabled="{Binding CanImportVideo}"
                  Click="OnImportVideoClick"
                  ToolTip.Tip="Choose a recorded meeting and transcribe its first audio stream" />
          <Button Classes="subtle"
                  Content="Cancel import"
                  IsVisible="{Binding IsImportingVideo}"
                  Command="{Binding CancelVideoImportCommand}"
                  ToolTip.Tip="Stop after preserving everything transcribed so far" />
        </Panel>

        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                    Spacing="{StaticResource Space3}"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    IsVisible="{Binding IsRecording}">
          <Ellipse Classes="pulse"
                   Width="{StaticResource RecordDotSize}"
                   Height="{StaticResource RecordDotSize}"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Fill="{DynamicResource DangerBase}"
                   ToolTip.Tip="{Binding Capture.RecordingStateText}" />
          <TextBlock Classes="mono"
                     VerticalAlignment="Center"
                     FontSize="{StaticResource FontSizeLg}"
                     TextTrimming="None"
                     Text="{Binding Capture.ElapsedText}" />
        </StackPanel>
      </Grid>

      <Button Grid.Column="7"
              Classes="record"
              Classes.rolling="{Binding IsRecording}"
              VerticalAlignment="Center"
              Content="{Binding RecordButtonText}"
              Command="{Binding ToggleRecordingCommand}"
              ToolTip.Tip="{Binding RecordButtonHint}" />
    </Grid>
  </Border>
</UserControl>
